  - dynamical systems
  - mathematical model
abstract: >-
  Python implementation, Colab notebooks, exported data and figure scripts for a minimal dynamical
  model of a periodontal site in which past inflammation shifts the host response threshold through a
  slowly recovering response state. After simulated therapy, inflammation resolves before
  responsiveness recovers, so treated sites respond to less plaque than never-diseased sites for months;
  an instantaneously adapting host with identical equilibria serves as control.
